        '### What PPCS Is — and Is Not',
        'Most concussions in adults resolve within 10–14 days; in children and adolescents the expected window extends to approximately 4 weeks (Amsterdam Consensus, Patricios et al., 2023). When symptoms persist beyond this expected timeframe, the patient is described as having persistent post-concussion symptoms — abbreviated PPCS.',
